# OPDP profile

What the website shows about a problem from its OPDP atlas record: difficulty and
tier, how well it fits current AI, tractability and the probability of progress,
the burden of formalizing and of verifying it, tool leverage, the recommended
route, the specialist hours the atlas estimates, and whether its text is a full
statement or an excerpt. A record is about 10 KB; the
profile keeps these few fields as display text, and the coordinator stores it in
the problem's `opdp` column.

Every value is kept as the atlas wrote it (`9.6`, `3-7%`, `T2`): the profile is
for reading, and the ranking that computes on the same numbers reads them exactly,
elsewhere. A field the record does not carry is the empty text, never zero.

## Note
The profile's keys, each with the path of the record field it shows.

## To opdpProfilePaths () -> Seq of Seq of Text:
    Let mutable out be [["difficultyLabel", "difficulty_label"], ["difficulty", "intrinsic_difficulty.score"], ["tier", "intrinsic_difficulty.tier_code"]].
    Push ["aiFit", "ai_assessment.fit_label"] to out.
    Push ["aiDifficulty", "ai_assessment.difficulty_score"] to out.
    Push ["tractability", "tractability.code"] to out.
    Push ["progress", "tractability.progress_probability.display_label"] to out.
    Push ["formalization", "formalization.score"] to out.
    Push ["verification", "verification.if_true_score"] to out.
    Push ["toolLeverage", "tool_leverage.score"] to out.
    Push ["route", "recommended_approach.route_label"] to out.
    Push ["effortHours", "human_attention.effort.estimated_specialist_hours.display_label"] to out.
    Push ["explanation", "explanation"] to out.
    Push ["gate", "assessment_gate.value"] to out.
    Push ["answerType", "classification.answer_type"] to out.
    Push ["proposalYear", "evidence.estimated_proposal_year"] to out.
    Push ["textMode", "source_text.text_mode"] to out.
    Return out.

## Note
The value at a dotted path as display text: a string as it is, a number as JSON
writes it, anything else (absent, null, an object) as the empty text.

## To opdpDisplay (v: Json, path: Text) -> Text:
    Let mutable here be v.
    Repeat for step in split(path, "."):
        Set here to jsonGet(here, step).
    Inspect here:
        When JStr (s):
            Return s.
        When JNum (n):
            Return jsonSerialize(here).
        When JDec (m, sc):
            Return jsonSerialize(here).
        Otherwise:
            Return "".
    Return "".

## Note
The profile of one record, as a compact JSON object of texts.

## To opdpProfile (v: Json) -> Text:
    Let mutable parts be a new Seq of Text.
    Repeat for pair in opdpProfilePaths():
        Push jsonQuote(item 1 of pair) + ":" + jsonQuote(opdpDisplay(v, item 2 of pair)) to parts.
    Return "{{" + join(parts, ",") + "}}".

## Note
The factory problem id a record profiles (`opdp:116`), or the empty text when the
record has no integer `problem_id`.

## To opdpProblemId (v: Json) -> Text:
    Inspect jsonGet(v, "problem_id"):
        When JNum (n):
            Return "opdp:{n}".
        Otherwise:
            Return "".
    Return "".

## Note
A small record in the atlas's shape, for the tests.

## To opdpSampleRecord (withTractability: Bool) -> Text:
    Let mutable t be "".
    If withTractability:
        Set t to ",\"tractability\":{{\"code\":\"T2\",\"progress_probability\":{{\"display_label\":\"3-7%\"}}}}".
    Return "{{\"problem_id\":116,\"difficulty_label\":\"T4 Hard\",\"intrinsic_difficulty\":{{\"score\":9.6,\"tier_code\":\"T4\"}},\"tool_leverage\":{{\"score\":8}}" + t + "}}".

## Test: opdp profiles keep the atlas display values

Let v be jsonParse(opdpSampleRecord(true)).
Expect that opdpProblemId(v) is equal to "opdp:116".
Expect that opdpDisplay(v, "intrinsic_difficulty.score") is equal to "9.6".
Expect that opdpDisplay(v, "tool_leverage.score") is equal to "8".
Expect that opdpDisplay(v, "tractability.progress_probability.display_label") is equal to "3-7%".
Expect that opdpDisplay(v, "intrinsic_difficulty") is equal to "".
Let profile be jsonParse(opdpProfile(v)).
Expect that jsonSerialize(jsonGet(profile, "tier")) is equal to "\"T4\"".
Expect that jsonSerialize(jsonGet(profile, "route")) is equal to "\"\"".
Expect that length of opdpProfilePaths() is equal to 17.

## Test: opdp profiles have no id without an integer problem id

Expect that opdpProblemId(jsonParse("{{\"problem_id\":\"116\"}}")) is equal to "".
Expect that opdpProblemId(jsonParse("[]")) is equal to "".

## Test: opdp profiles show an absent field as empty

For all booleans present:
    Let profile be opdpProfile(jsonParse(opdpSampleRecord(present))).
    Expect that jsonValid(profile) is equal to true.
    Expect that (profile contains "\"progress\":\"3-7%\"") is equal to present.
